# Accepted-risk CVEs for this image's Trivy scans (local pre-push hook and
# CI, both --severity CRITICAL,HIGH). See docs/SECURITY.md's "Accepted-risk
# CVEs" section for the full reasoning; the short version is below.
#
# gocryptfs is the only Go binary in this image, installed via `apk add
# gocryptfs~=${GOCRYPTFS_VERSION}` (see Dockerfile). Its upstream release
# (v2.6.1, the latest as of this writing) still pins golang.org/x/crypto
# v0.33.0 and was built with Go 1.26.3; gocryptfs's `master` branch has
# already bumped to x/crypto v0.52.0 and Go 1.25.0, but no release has
# shipped with that bump yet. All CVE IDs below are upstream, in gocryptfs's
# own vendored dependencies, with no fix available on our side until
# gocryptfs cuts a release off that branch.
#
# Docker Scout's SBOM-based scan (see .github/workflows/publish-image.yml)
# flags these. A plain `trivy image` scan of this image currently does NOT:
# Trivy tracks gocryptfs purely as the Alpine apk package
# (gocryptfs 2.6.1-r5) once it is apk-installed, and does not separately run
# its gobinary analyzer against a binary a distro package manager already
# owns, so the vendored x/crypto/stdlib versions embedded in the binary
# itself never surface through `trivy image`. Confirmed 2026-09-06 by
# extracting /usr/bin/gocryptfs from the built image and scanning it
# directly with `trivy rootfs`, which does run the gobinary analyzer and
# reports exactly the CVE IDs listed below for golang.org/x/crypto v0.33.0
# and stdlib v1.26.3, plus a handful of MEDIUM/UNKNOWN-severity findings
# (CVE-2026-39833, CVE-2026-39834, CVE-2026-56855, CVE-2026-78662, and
# others) that fall outside the CRITICAL,HIGH gate this repo enforces and so
# are not listed here.
#
# These entries are kept here anyway, as the canonical accepted-risk record,
# in case Trivy's detection scope changes (a future version that does scan
# apk-owned Go binaries, or a `--pkg-types` change) or a downstream
# `trivy image` invocation with different flags does surface them.
#
# Do NOT add util-linux (libblkid/libmount) CVEs here. Those are a
# transitive base-layer package fixed upstream by Alpine (util-linux
# 2.42.3-r1 on the 3.24 branch as of this writing); the Dockerfile's
# `apk update && apk upgrade` picks the fix up on every rebuild, so they
# should keep failing a scan against a stale image until it is rebuilt,
# which is the point of running these scans at all.
#
# Adding a new entry here requires the same rigor as this list: confirm it
# against a live `trivy image` (or `trivy rootfs` against the extracted
# binary, per the note above) run or a current Docker Scout scan of the
# actual image, not a copy-paste from an advisory feed or a prior list.

# golang.org/x/crypto (embedded in gocryptfs, pinned to v0.33.0 upstream)
CVE-2025-22869
